## Security Best Practices (Real-time Multiplayer / Socket.IO)

### Current Posture
| Layer | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| **Supply Chain** | ✅ Hardened | `minimumReleaseAge: 1440` in pnpm-workspace.yaml |
| **Input Validation** | ⚠️ Partial | Phase/alive/role checks but **no Zod schemas** on socket events |
| **Rate Limiting** | ❌ Missing | No per-socket/per-IP limits |
| **Auth/Identity** | ❌ Anonymous | Socket.id only; no signed tokens |
| **Information Hiding** | ⚠️ **LEAK** | `serializePlayers()` sends `isHost` to ALL clients |
| **Room Isolation** | ✅ Enforced | Socket.join(code) |
| **Privilege Checks** | ✅ Server-side | Validated on server |
| **DoS Protection** | ❌ Missing | No max rooms/IP, max players/room |

### Critical Vulnerability: Host Identity Leak
**File**: `artifacts/api-server/src/socket-handlers.ts:64-73`
```typescript
function serializePlayers(players: Map<string, Player>, revealRoles = false) {
  return Array.from(players.values()).map((p) => ({
    id: p.id,
    name: p.name,
    isHost: p.isHost,        // ❌ SENT TO EVERYONE
    alive: p.alive,
    connected: p.connected,
    ...(revealRoles ? { role: p.role } : {}),
  }));
}
```
**Impact**: Every player receives full player list with `isHost: true/false`

### Recommended Enhancements (Priority Order)
1. **Fix host leak** — Per-recipient serialization (current task)
2. **Add Zod schemas** — Validate all socket event payloads
3. **Rate limiting** — Max events/sec per socket
4. **Signed room tokens** — JWT for reconnection
5. **Connection limits** — Max 50 players/room, max 10 rooms/IP
6. **Audit logging** — Privileged actions (kick, start-game)
7. **Content Security Policy** — Helmet.js for HTTP routes

