## Forward-Looking Notes & Recommendations

### Animation Libraries
- **Framer Motion** (12.23.24) — Already in use, fits React/Tailwind for complex/layout animations
- **Tailwind-animate** (`tw-animate-css` 1.4.0) — For simple CSS micro-interactions
- **CSS Animations** — Native, zero deps (typewriter, pulse, fade-in)
- **Future considerations**:
  - **Motion One** (`@motionone/react`) — WAAPI-based, lighter than Framer
  - **React Spring** — Spring physics, drag gestures (PlayerCircle reorder)
  - **Anime.js** — Timeline sequences (phase transitions)
  - **Lottie React** — Designer animations (requires .json files)
- **Guideline**: Prefer Framer Motion for React-integrated; tw-animate-css for Tailwind-native; CSS for loops/simple transitions

### Mobile App Packaging (Android APK / iOS via Capacitor)
- **Capacitor** highly recommended — seamless Vite/React integration
- **Feasibility**:
  - React 19 + Vite ✅
  - Socket.io-client ✅ (works in Capacitor WebView)
  - Web Audio API ✅
  - Express Backend ❌ (must run on external server)
  - WebSocket (ws/wss) ✅ (requires `wss://` in production)

**Setup Template**:
```bash
pnpm add -D @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli @capacitor/android @capacitor/ios
npx cap init mafia-wars com.mafiawars.app --web-dir=artifacts/game-lobby/dist
npx cap add android
npx cap add ios
```

**capacitor.config.ts**:
```typescript
{
  appId: 'com.mafiawars.app',
  appName: 'Mafia Wars',
  webDir: 'artifacts/game-lobby/dist',
  server: { url: 'http://LAN_IP:5173', cleartext: true },
  android: { allowMixedContent: true },
  plugins: { CapacitorHttp: { enabled: true }, PushNotifications: {} }
}
```

**Required Backend Changes for Mobile**:
- CORS: Allow `capacitor://localhost`, `http://localhost`, production domain
- WebSocket proxy (nginx): `proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;`
- SSL: `wss://` required for production

